# Thrifted Rug — extended palette
#
# base24 has 24 slots. This palette is 5 accent FAMILIES x 3 shades
# (deep / primary / light) plus neutrals and functional roles.
#
# base24 covers the PRIMARY shades (normal ANSI) and the LIGHT shades
# (bright ANSI). The DEEP shades have no base24 slot — they live here,
# for custom templates that want hover/active states or richer UI layering.
#
# Everything below is DERIVED FROM OR CONSISTENT WITH schemes/thrifted-rug.yaml.
# That file is the source of truth for anything base24 can express.
# Change a colour there first; only add here what base24 cannot hold.

# --- deep accent shades (no base24 slot) --------------------------------
GREEN_DEEP='#5c7c58'      # deep forest      — active/pressed states
ROSE_DEEP='#8e5568'       # deeper burgundy
TEAL_DEEP='#4f8d84'       # darker teal
LAVENDER_DEEP='#5d6f9e'   # deeper lavender-blue
# NOTE: Deep Gold #b3894f is used as base09 (Orange), so it is NOT repeated here.

# --- semantic roles ------------------------------------------------------
# Aliases onto base24 slots. Templates should reference ROLES, not colour
# families, so a future theme with e.g. a rose primary is a remap here
# rather than an edit to every template.
ACCENT='#8fb573'          # base0B — main highlights, selections
ACCENT_HOVER='#a8c498'    # base14 — light variant for hover
ACCENT_ACTIVE='#5c7c58'   # GREEN_DEEP — deep variant for active/pressed

ERROR='#c67676'           # base08
WARNING='#d4a373'         # base0A
SUCCESS='#76b0a6'         # base0C
INFO='#8a98c6'            # base0D
SPECIAL='#a37d63'         # base0F — debug / deprecated

# --- usage philosophy (from the original README) -------------------------
# * background colours for UI layering, darkest to lightest
# * primary green for main highlights and selections
# * accent families for visual categorisation and variety
# * functional colours for consistent status indicators
# * LIGHT variants for hover, DEEP variants for active/pressed
